# Mizano ERP — AI Assistant Rules

## Project Overview
AI-powered ERP (Autonomous Accounting Platform). Zero-touch accounting — AI handles 95% of work. No accounting knowledge required.
Key concepts: Zero-Day Close, Perpetual General Ledger, Human-in-the-Loop.

### Tech Stack
| Layer    | Technology                                            |
| -------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |
| Frontend | Next.js 14 (App Router), React 18, TypeScript         |
| Backend  | NestJS 10, TypeScript strict                          |
| Database | PostgreSQL 16 + Prisma ORM                            |
| Queue    | Redis + BullMQ                                        |
| UI       | shadcn/ui + Tailwind CSS + Radix UI + Lucide          |
| Charts   | Recharts                                              |
| State    | TanStack Query (server) + Zustand (client)            |
| Forms    | React Hook Form + Zod                                 |
| Auth     | NextAuth.js (frontend) + JWT refresh tokens (backend) |
| AI       | Ollama (100% local LLM inference)                     |
| Monorepo | Turborepo + pnpm workspaces                           |

## Architecture Principles

1. **Multi-tenancy** — ALL queries MUST include `organizationId`. Never leak data across orgs.
2. **Double-entry accounting** — Debits MUST equal credits. Throw if unbalanced.
3. **Money** — ALWAYS `Decimal` (Prisma `@db.Decimal(19, 4)`). NEVER JS `number`/`float` for money.
4. **Soft delete** — Financial records use `deletedAt`, never hard delete.
5. **Audit trail** — Every write creates an audit log entry automatically.
6. **AI is advisory** — NEVER auto-post transactions. All AI suggestions are dismissible.
7. **Modular monolith** — Each business domain is a separate NestJS module and Next.js route group. Modules communicate via service injection.
8. **Type-safe end-to-end** — Share types via `packages/shared-types`, validation via `packages/validators`.
9. **FIFO inventory valuation** — All stock movements use First-In First-Out costing.

## Code Style & Conventions

### Backend (NestJS) — apps/api/

- One module per business domain: `src/modules/{domain}/`
- Module structure: `{domain}.module.ts`, `{domain}.controller.ts`, `{domain}.service.ts`, `dto/`
- Use NestJS dependency injection — never instantiate services manually
- ALL endpoints protected by `JwtAuthGuard` + `OrganizationGuard` (except auth routes)
- Use `@Permissions('module.action')` decorator for RBAC checks
- Standardized responses: `{ data: T, meta?: { page, limit, total, totalPages } }`
- Use Prisma interactive transactions (`prisma.$transaction()`) for multi-table writes
- Monetary values: ALWAYS `Decimal` from Prisma, NEVER JavaScript `number` or `float`
- Auto-generate document numbers per org: INV-XXX, EST-XXX, JRN-XXX, BILL-XXX, etc.
- Error responses: `{ statusCode, message, error, details?: fieldErrors }`
- Cron jobs via `@nestjs/schedule` for: recurring transactions, overdue status updates, AI analysis

### Frontend (Next.js) — apps/web/

- App Router with route groups: `(auth)` for login/register, `(dashboard)` for protected pages
- React Server Components by default. Add `'use client'` ONLY for interactive components
- Page structure: `app/[locale]/(dashboard)/{module}/page.tsx` for list, `[id]/page.tsx` for detail
- Module components: `components/{module}/` — module-specific UI
- Shared components: `components/ui/` — shadcn/ui primitives
- Data fetching: TanStack Query hooks in `lib/hooks/use-{resource}.ts`
- API client: typed functions in `lib/api.ts` using fetch
- Forms: react-hook-form + zodResolver with schemas from `packages/validators`
- Tables: TanStack Table (`@tanstack/react-table`) for ALL data tables
- Every page must handle: loading skeleton, error state, empty state
- Toast notifications via sonner for success/error feedback
- Use `next/navigation` for routing (useRouter, redirect)
- Responsive design: mobile-first with Tailwind breakpoints
- Dark mode support via next-themes
- i18n: `next-intl` with messages in `messages/{locale}/`

### Database (Prisma) — apps/api/prisma/

- All models: `id String @id @default(cuid())`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt`, `organizationId`
- Financial models add: `deletedAt DateTime?` for soft delete
- Money fields: `Decimal @db.Decimal(19, 4)`
- Use Prisma enums for all statuses and types
- Composite indexes on: `[organizationId, status]`, `[organizationId, createdAt]`
- Relations with explicit foreign keys and appropriate cascade rules
- After schema changes: `pnpm db:generate`

## Business Domain Modules

| Module        | Path                     | Key Entities                                          |
| ------------- | ------------------------ | ----------------------------------------------------- |
| Accounting    | `modules/accounting/`    | Accounts, Journals, RecurringProfiles                 |
| Sales         | `modules/sales/`         | Customers, Quotes, Invoices, CreditNotes, Payments    |
| Purchases     | `modules/purchases/`     | Vendors, Bills, Expenses, VendorCredits               |
| Inventory     | `modules/inventory/`     | Items, Warehouses, Movements, Adjustments, PriceLists |
| Banking       | `modules/banking/`       | BankAccounts, Transactions, Rules                     |
| HR            | `modules/hr/`            | Employees, Attendance, PayrollRuns, Payslips          |
| Manufacturing | `modules/manufacturing/` | BOMs, WorkOrders                                      |
| Projects      | `modules/projects/`      | Projects, Tasks, TimesheetEntries                     |
| Tax           | `modules/tax/`           | TaxRates, VATReturns, VATPayments                     |
| CRM           | `modules/crm/`           | Leads, Deals                                          |
| Reports       | `modules/reports/`       | P&L, Balance Sheet, AR/AP Aging, Dashboard            |
| AI            | `modules/ai/`            | Ollama-backed inference (extraction, predictions)     |
| Assets        | `modules/assets/`        | FixedAssets, Depreciation                             |
| Documents     | `modules/documents/`     | Document management                                   |
| Currency      | `modules/currency/`      | Exchange rates, multi-currency                        |
| Notifications | `modules/notifications/` | In-app & email notifications                          |
| Search        | `modules/search/`        | Global search                                         |
| Import/Export | `modules/import-export/` | CSV/Excel import & export                             |
| Audit         | `modules/audit/`         | Activity & audit trail                                |
| Bulk Ops      | `modules/bulk-operations/`| Bulk actions on records                               |

### Sales Flow
Customer -> Quote (EST-XXX) -> Invoice (INV-XXX) -> Payment Received
- Credit Note (CN-XXX): linked to invoice, reverses AR and VAT
- Delivery Challan (DC-XXX): decreases stock
- Recurring Invoices: auto-generate on schedule

### Purchases Flow
Vendor -> Bill (BILL-XXX) / Expense -> Payment Made
- Vendor Credit: mirror of Credit Note, apply to bills or refund
- Recurring bills and expenses supported

### Inventory
- Item types: Goods (tracked), Service (no stock), Digital
- FIFO valuation, multi-warehouse, composite items (bundles)
- Adjustments: Loss: Dr Shrinkage / Cr Inventory. Gain: Dr Inventory / Cr Income.

### Banking
- Account types: Bank, Credit Card, Petty Cash
- Statement import: CSV/Excel/OFX parsing
- AI Reconciliation: direction check -> exact amount -> reference parsing -> fuzzy name matching -> confidence scoring

### Manufacturing
- BOM: recipe with output item + input materials + operations cost
- Work Orders (WO-XXX): material needs, stock check, production completion

### Projects
- Billing methods: Fixed, Project Hourly, Task Hourly, Staff Hourly
- Timesheets: timer widget + manual entry, billable tracking
- Project invoicing: unbilled hours, expenses, or fixed installments

## AI Module (src/modules/ai/)

### Architecture
- **Ollama-backed**: All AI features use local Ollama LLM inference via `OllamaInferenceGateway`
- **No training**: Inference-only — no model training, retraining, or fine-tuning infrastructure
- **No OCR/VLM microservices**: Removed. Document extraction uses Ollama vision/text models directly
- **Document classification**: Naive Bayes via `natural` library in `document-classification.service.ts`

### AI Services
- `ollama-inference-gateway.service.ts` — Central gateway for all Ollama model calls
- `ollama.service.ts` — Low-level Ollama API client
- `document-intake.service.ts` — Document upload, extraction via Ollama
- `entity-extraction.service.ts` — Extract structured data from documents
- `cash-flow-prediction.service.ts` — Cash flow forecasting
- `payment-prediction.service.ts` — Payment behavior prediction
- Prompts defined in `prompts/ollama-extraction.prompts.ts`

### AI Business Rules
- **Never auto-post**: All financial suggestions require explicit user confirmation
- **Confidence scoring**: Every AI prediction includes a confidence score (0-1)
- **Human-in-the-Loop**: All suggestions are dismissible — user has final say
- **Reconciliation confidence**: > 0.8 = high (green), > 0.6 = medium (yellow), else = low (red)
- **Anomaly detection**: z-score > 3 = warning, z-score > 4 = critical alert
- Background processing: AI analysis runs in background jobs, not blocking UI

## API Design Conventions

- RESTful: GET (list/detail), POST (create), PATCH (update), DELETE (soft delete)
- List endpoints: `?page=1&limit=20&sortBy=createdAt&sortOrder=desc`
- Cursor pagination supported for large datasets
- Filtering: `?status=OPEN&dateFrom=2026-01-01&dateTo=2026-01-31&customerId=xxx`
- Search: `?search=keyword` (searches relevant text fields)
- Include relations: `?include=customer,items,payments`
- Bulk operations: POST `/{resource}/bulk` with array body

## Error Handling

- Backend: Global exception filter. Format: `{ statusCode, message, error, timestamp, path }`
- Validation errors: `{ statusCode: 400, message: 'Validation failed', details: { field: 'error' } }`
- Business rules: descriptive messages (e.g., "Cannot delete customer with 5 existing invoices")
- Frontend: Error boundaries per route segment. Toast for transient errors. Inline for form errors.

## Security

- JWT access tokens (15min) + refresh tokens (7d)
- RBAC checked on every protected endpoint
- Organization isolation on every database query
- Input sanitization (strip HTML, validate types)
- Rate limiting on auth endpoints
- CORS restricted to frontend origin
- Helmet headers on NestJS
- Prisma parameterized queries (SQL injection safe)
- File upload validation (type, size limits)
- Audit log for compliance

## CI & Quality

`pnpm ci:full` MUST pass with **ZERO warnings and ZERO errors**.

### Lint rules
- No `eslint-disable` without justification
- No unused imports/variables (prefix unused params with `_`)
- No `any` — use proper types, `unknown`, or generics
- No `console.log` — use NestJS Logger in backend
- All promises must be awaited, `.catch()`ed, or `void`ed
- Always `const`; only `let` when reassignment needed
- ES module imports only (`import`, not `require`)

### Type-check rules
- Explicit return types on all exported functions
- `strict: true` — no implicit `any`
- `Decimal` for all monetary values, never `number`
- No `@ts-ignore` without explanation comment

### Test rules
- All existing tests must pass after changes
- Mock Redis, external APIs — no infra dependency in unit tests
- When modifying business logic, update/add corresponding tests
- API tests: `node apps/api/_run_tests.js [--testPathPattern="<pattern>"]`
- Web tests: `cd apps/web && npx jest [--testPathPattern="<pattern>"]`

### Git Hooks
- **pre-commit**: lint-staged (ESLint --fix + Prettier on staged files)
- **pre-push**: `pnpm ci:full` — all checks must pass

## Quick Commands

```bash
pnpm dev              # Web :5001 + API :6001
pnpm dev:api / dev:web
pnpm build / lint / type-check
pnpm db:generate / db:push / db:migrate / db:seed / db:studio
pnpm test / test:api / test:cov / test:e2e / test:playwright
pnpm ci:full          # lint + type-check + test + e2e (MUST pass)
pnpm docker:up / docker:down / docker:prod
pnpm env:check        # verify env file for current APP_ENV
```

## Environment System (4-env)

| File         | APP_ENV | NODE_ENV    | Purpose             |
| ------------ | ------- | ----------- | ------------------- |
| `.env.local` | local   | development | Local dev (default) |
| `.env.dev`   | dev     | development | Shared dev server   |
| `.env.sit`   | sit     | production  | Integration testing |
| `.env.prod`  | prod    | production  | Production          |

